    L1  0.5°E – 0.55°E, 0.5°N – 0.55°N, 5.6 km a side. The origin is on its west side at 0.525°N.
    L2  0.47°E – 0.58°E, 0.47°N – 0.58°N, 12.2 km a side: 3.3 km out from L1 on every side.

  A spoke joins L1 to L2 along 0.525°N, from 0.55°E to 0.58°E (3.3 km), tagged maxspeed=4. Each corner of a loop has
  a stub of road 0.8 km long, inwards for L1 and outwards for L2, so the builder keeps the corner: it collapses a
  chain of nodes no other road meets into one straight edge.

  0.01° is 1.112 km here: 0.0222 h of travel at 60 km/h. From the origin, L1 is reached within 0.222 h (0.1° round
  either way to the spoke). The spoke takes 3.336 km at 4 km/h × 1.2 = 1.001 h, so L2 is reached from 1.223 h (at
  the spoke) to 1.712 h (its west side at 0.525°N, 0.22° round either way): all of it in the 2 h ring, none in 1 h.

  The land up to 1 km from a road is in the ring with it, so in 1 h L1 walls in 3.6 × 3.6 km = 13 km² of land: ring 1
  holds all of L1 and the land in it. In 2 h L1 and L2 wall in the land between them, a band 1.3 km wide, ~46 km²:
  ring 2 holds it, and all round the land of ring 1, 7.6 × 7.6 km = 57 km², which is not in ring 2.

